#!/usr/bin/env perl
use 5.014;
use strict;
use warnings;

use Game::Snake::Terminal;

our $VERSION = '0.13';

exit Game::Snake::Terminal->run(@ARGV);

__END__

=head1 NAME

snake - the classic snake game, in a terminal or a window

=head1 SYNOPSIS

    snake                      # play, the board fitted to the window
    snake --cols 20 --rows 14  # a smaller board
    snake --watch --level 3    # watch the bot
    snake --raylib             # a window, when Raylib::FFI is installed
    snake --help

=head1 DESCRIPTION

Steer with the arrows, wasd or hjkl; p pauses; q quits. The snake grows by
one for each piece of food and speeds up as the score doubles. It dies at a
wall or on its own body.

The keys need L<Term::ReadKey>. Without it the game says so and exits 2;
C<--watch> works anywhere.

=head1 EXIT STATUS

0 when a game ended or was quit; 2 for a bad option, or a game that could not
start.

=head1 SEE ALSO

L<Game::Snake::Terminal>, which this program is two lines over.

